docs/design-concepts

# Secrets must not enter the build context. `Dockerfile` does `COPY . .`, and the ROOT `.env`
# is the file docker-compose.yml and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md tell every operator to create
# (`cp .env.example .env`) — it holds SECRET_KEY, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, ADMIN_SECRET,
# DIVERA_ACCESS_KEY, TRACCAR_PASSWORD, VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY and STT_API_KEY. Only `backend/.env`
# was listed here, so a source build baked the real one into an image layer and into any
# exported build cache. The pattern now covers both, and `.env.example` is explicitly kept
# because it is documentation and carries no values.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
